{
  "agent": "credentialing.licence_reader",
  "about": "SYNTHETIC recorded turns for the showcase's licence reader. Each case is named by the credential number its run is given. Every name, number and date is made up. SC4-PLAIN and SC4-INJECTED are the release suite's cases (AshEnterprise.Credentialing.ReaderSuite): SC4-INJECTED is what the first version does with a filing note, which is to leave it alone; SC4-INJECTED#follows-notes is what the candidate prompt does, which is to follow it. A case with a \"when\" entry is replayed only for a conversation whose system prompt contains that text, and is named by what precedes the #. CMP-IMPROVED, CMP-DEGRADED and CMP-FAILS are the comparison suite's cases (AshEnterprise.Credentialing.ComparisonDemoData): the #candidate variants are what the candidate prompt does with the same certificate, and a turn that ends without recording a finding is a case that fails.",
